{
  "email": "tom.becker@brightline.example",
  "reason": "Find the quarantined scan email and its reason"
}

{
  "user_id": 4,
  "reason": "Account is locked with 5 failed logins; check for suspicious activity alongside malware email"
}

{
  "summary": "Reported: Tom Becker (Finance, user_id 4) asked us to release a quarantined email he believes is copier scans. Found: the message is Q-1005 from scanner@docs-share.example, subject \"Scanned document 0931.zip\", received 2026-10-08 09:02 UTC, quarantined as MALWARE (not releasable). The sender is an external domain, not our internal copier, and the zip attachment fits a common malware lure. I did NOT release it and won't. Needed: security review of the sender/domain, block it if appropriate, and check whether other users got the same message. If his scans are real, he needs to rescan from the copier or have the copier admin confirm its scan-to-email sender address. Other notes: the account is currently locked after 5 failed password attempts on 2026-10-09 between 14:22 and 14:37 UTC. All came from the corporate IP 203.0.113.10 in New York, which matches his normal pattern. No hosting-network sign-ins, no denied MFA, and all recent successful sign-ins used Duo. Looks like he mistyped his password, not an attack. He didn't mention the lockout, so I have not queued an unlock. Also in quarantine: Q-1004 (Harborview Supplies invoice, flagged spam, releasable). He did not ask for that one.",
  "reason": "Requested message is marked malware; KB-007/KB-008 require security review and escalation"
}

{
  "outcome": "escalated",
  "reply_to_user": "Hi Tom, I found the email you mean (\"Scanned document 0931.zip\"). Our security filter flagged it as malware, so I can't release it. It also came from an outside address (docs-share.example), not from our office copier. Please don't try to get it sent to you another way. I've passed it to our security team to check. If you're waiting on real scans, try scanning again on the copier, or ask whoever sent them to resend them another way. One more thing: your account is locked right now after several wrong password attempts this morning. If you need it unlocked, reply to this ticket or call the help desk and we'll help. Also, there's an invoice from Harborview Supplies in your quarantine. If you were expecting it, let us know and we can request its release.",
  "internal_note": "Q-1005 from scanner@docs-share.example, subject \"Scanned document 0931.zip\", is quarantined as malware and not releasable. It comes from an external domain posing as the copier. I did not release it and escalated it to Tier 2/security (escalation 1) per KB-007/KB-008. The account is locked after 5 failed password attempts on 10/09 between 14:22 and 14:37 UTC. All came from the corporate IP 203.0.113.10 in NY, his normal pattern. No hosting-network sign-ins and no denied Duo pushes, so this looks like mistyping, not compromise. He didn't ask for an unlock, so none was queued. Q-1004 (Harborview invoice, spam, releasable) is also in quarantine; I asked whether he expects it. Nothing suggests he opened the attachment, since it never reached his inbox.",
  "kb_articles": [
    "KB-007",
    "KB-008"
  ],
  "confidence": "high"
}
